accTitle: Supply-chain request and simulation boundary
accDescr: The agent interprets a request, reads modeled facts, and proposes a typed candidate. Read-only candidates use perception actions that return versioned observations with provenance. State-changing candidates pass workflow approval when required and the action boundary before a typed command is applied by the deterministic simulator to the current modeled world. Figure 19.4 expands the individual approval, capability, idempotency, and version gates.
    User[User request] --> Agent[Agent interprets request, reads facts, and proposes]
    Agent --> Candidate[Typed candidate action]
    Candidate --> Kind{Read-only or<br/>state-changing?}
    Kind -->|Read-only| Perception[Perception action returns a<br/>versioned observation with provenance]
    Perception --> Agent
    Kind -->|State-changing| Gate[Workflow approval when required;<br/>action dispatch and version checks]
    Gate --> Simulator[Deterministic simulator applies<br/>a typed command to the current modeled world]
    Simulator --> Result[New snapshot and typed effects]
    Result --> Agent
